{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgqiirrKoxZZutsJHwuYh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I couldn't open the source, so this diagnosis comes from the symbol names and line numbers in the retrieved graph. The line ranges are estimates.\n\nThe most likely cause is in `AuthService.getTokensData`. It signs both the access token and the refresh token, and the refresh token almost certainly gets the short access-token `expiresIn` (from `auth.expires`) instead of `auth.refreshExpires`. That would give a refresh token whose `exp` is only minutes after `iat`. `JwtRefreshStrategy` would then reject it once that lifetime passes, which matches the 401s.\n\nThe second candidate is `auth.config.ts`, where the refresh lifetime may be read from the wrong environment variable. The third is `AuthService.refreshToken`, which re-issues tokens through `getTokensData` and so inherits the same problem. I rank both below the first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12382,"cache_read_input_tokens":791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12382},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e957de64-ddfa-48a4-9496-af178ac50a12","uuid":"13a11611-b818-4b2d-9be7-576483dd586b","timestamp":"2026-11-08T15:45:37.226Z","request_id":"req_011CgqiiregGd9RYhThAS2w7"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgqiirrKoxZZutsJHwuYh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017WZSLwSPMLpojJNwqjTP7e","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"candidates":[{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.getTokensData","start_line":599,"end_line":640,"explanation":"The refresh token is signed with the access token lifetime (auth.expires / tokenExpiresIn) instead of auth.refreshExpires, so its exp is only minutes after iat regardless of AUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN=30d. JwtRefreshStrategy then rejects it once that short lifetime passes, giving 401 on /auth/refresh."},{"file":"src/auth/config/auth.config.ts","symbol":"registerAs(auth)","start_line":1,"end_line":40,"explanation":"If refreshExpires is read from the wrong env var (e.g. AUTH_JWT_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN), the refresh lifetime would ignore AUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN."},{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","symbol":"AuthService.refreshToken","start_line":523,"end_line":560,"explanation":"Re-issues tokens through getTokensData, so the short refresh lifetime is propagated on every refresh. Less likely to be the root cause."}],"fix":{"file":"src/auth/auth.service.ts","description":"In getTokensData, sign the refresh token with expiresIn from configService.getOrThrow('auth.refreshExpires', { infer: true }) rather than the access token expiry. Check that auth.config.ts maps refreshExpires to AUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN."}},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12382,"cache_read_input_tokens":791,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12382},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e957de64-ddfa-48a4-9